-- The Linux window backend (`--windows wayland`): ghostty-agent is itself a
-- headless Wayland compositor built on wlroots, and the game is its only
-- display. The plugin runs inside FFXIV under Wine, a Windows PE process that
-- can neither host a Unix-socket Wayland server nor load Linux libraries, so
-- the compositor lives here in the Linux-native agent. Apps started into it
-- (WOPEN "run:CMD") or any client pointed at its socket become windows;
-- their pixels stream to the game as world panels and the game's pointer and
-- keys come back through the compositor's wlr_seat. Nothing touches the host
-- desktop: no portal, no picker, no host compositor involvement.
--
-- Pieces: one wl_display whose event loop the agent's main loop polls; the
-- headless backend; the pixman renderer (software: frames land in CPU memory,
-- which is what we stream, and no GPU is needed); compositor, subcompositor,
-- data device, primary selection, viewporter, xdg-shell and xdg-decoration
-- (always server side: the game panel draws the chrome). Every xdg_toplevel
-- gets its own wlr_scene and its own headless output sized to the window's
-- geometry; rendering that output yields the window's pixels. Popups render
-- into their toplevel's scene.
--
-- X11 apps come in through wlroots' Xwayland (started with the first X11
-- client): their toplevels are windows like xdg ones, their override-redirect
-- windows (menus, tooltips) are drawn into the window they belong to.
--
-- A window's picture is the window and its popups: menus may reach outside
-- the window (by up to POPUP_MARGIN), the picture grows to hold them and
-- CaptureFrame.boxes says where the window is in it (WGEOM).
--
-- Limits (docs/REMOTE_WINDOWS.md): TEXT typed
-- through keymap lookup (levels 1 and 2 of the layout; other characters are
-- dropped), software rendering only.
--
-- Loaded by agent/capture.nelua when the agent was built with -D WAYLAND
-- (tools/wayland-flags.sh: vendor/wayland-sdk headers, host libwlroots-0.20).
require 'string'
require 'stringbuilder'
require 'vector'
require 'memory'
require 'io'
require 'os'
require 'math'
require 'core.protocol'
require 'agent.wayland_keys'
require 'agent.desktop_entries'
require 'agent.browser'

